---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';

/*
 * Placeholder. The consent checkbox in step 3 links here, so this page must
 * exist — a consent control pointing at a 404 is worse than no link at all.
 *
 * This is deliberately NOT a privacy policy. Writing one would mean inventing
 * the controller's identity, retention periods and legal basis (CLAUDE.md 12).
 * What follows is only a factual statement of what the form collects, which is
 * verifiable from the code. The real policy must cover BOTH UK and EU GDPR,
 * because the business serves customers across Europe (CLAUDE.md 11), and the
 * site must not launch without it.
 */
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — [AWAITING COPY: trading name]"
  description="How enquiry details submitted through this site are used."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-page px-gutter pt-section pb-section">
    <h1 class="max-w-content font-serif text-heading text-ink">Privacy</h1>

    <div class="mt-6 max-w-content rounded-sm border border-line-strong bg-surface p-6">
      <p class="font-medium text-ink">
        [AWAITING: full privacy policy, covering both UK GDPR and EU GDPR.]
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-muted">
        This site must not go live until this page carries a real policy. See
        MISSING-ASSETS.md section 6.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-10 font-serif text-xl text-ink">What the enquiry form collects</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-content text-ink-muted">
      Accurate as of the current build, and limited to what is needed to reply with a quote:
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-4 max-w-content list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-ink-muted">
      <li>Your name, phone number and email address</li>
      <li>Your country and postcode, so we can quote for delivery</li>
      <li>The appliances you asked about — the link or model number you sent, and any note</li>
      <li>
        Context about the enquiry itself: which brands you opened, the page you arrived on, and how
        long it took to fill in
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-content text-ink-muted">
      No full address, no date of birth, and no marketing sign-up. The site sets no cookies and
      uses no advertising or tracking tags, which is why you have not been asked to accept any.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 font-serif text-xl text-ink">Counting visits</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-content text-ink-muted">
      We count page views and a small number of actions — which step of the enquiry form people
      reach, which brands they open, whether sending an enquiry succeeded — so we can see where
      the site is failing people. It is measured with a cookieless tool
      [AWAITING: analytics provider name]: no cookie is set, no identifier is stored on your
      device, and nothing measured here includes your name, contact details or what you asked
      about.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 font-serif text-xl text-ink">Checking your postcode</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-content text-ink-muted">
      If you give a UK postcode, your browser sends it to
      <a
        href="https://postcodes.io"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4">postcodes.io</a
      >, a free service built on Office for National Statistics open data, so we can show you the
      town it belongs to and confirm you typed it correctly. Only the postcode is sent — never your
      name, contact details or enquiry. We do not look up or store your street address.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 font-serif text-xl text-ink">Sending your enquiry</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-content text-ink-muted">
      When you press send, your browser passes the enquiry to
      <a
        href="https://web3forms.com"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4">Web3Forms</a
      >, a form-delivery service, which forwards it to us as an email. It is the only third party
      that handles your contact details.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-content text-ink-muted">
      If you choose to send your enquiry on WhatsApp instead, that message is handled by WhatsApp
      under their own terms, not ours.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 font-serif text-xl text-ink">Where it is held</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-content text-ink-muted">
      Your unfinished enquiry is kept in your own browser so you can come back to it, and is
      discarded after 30 days or as soon as it is sent. You can clear it at any time with
      &ldquo;Start again&rdquo; on the enquiry page.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-content text-ink-muted">
      If an enquiry cannot be sent — you are offline, or the service is down — it stays in your
      browser and we try again the next time you open the page, so that it is not lost. It is
      removed as soon as it goes through, and in any case after 30 days.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 font-serif text-xl text-ink">Contact</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-content text-ink-muted">{site.contact.email}</p>
  </div>
</Base>
